# Environment Configuration Template

## Backend Environment Variables (.env)

```
# Gemini API Configuration
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# JWT Configuration
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key_change_in_production_12345678901234567890
JWT_EXPIRATION=86400000

# Database Configuration
DATABASE_URL=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/aasa_db
DATABASE_USER=aasa_user
DATABASE_PASSWORD=aasa_password
DATABASE_DRIVER=org.postgresql.Driver

# Server Configuration
SERVER_PORT=8080
SERVER_SERVLET_CONTEXT_PATH=/

# JPA/Hibernate Configuration
JPA_HIBERNATE_DDL_AUTO=update
JPA_SHOW_SQL=false
JPA_PROPERTIES_HIBERNATE_FORMAT_SQL=true

# File Upload Configuration
FILE_UPLOAD_DIR=uploads/pdfs
FILE_MAX_SIZE=52428800

# CORS Configuration
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173
CORS_ALLOWED_METHODS=GET,POST,PUT,DELETE,OPTIONS
CORS_ALLOWED_HEADERS=*
CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS=true

# Logging Configuration
LOGGING_LEVEL_ROOT=INFO
LOGGING_LEVEL_COM_AASA=DEBUG
LOGGING_LEVEL_ORG_SPRINGFRAMEWORK_SECURITY=DEBUG

# Gemini Model Configuration
GEMINI_MODEL_NAME=gemini-1.5-flash
```

## Frontend Environment Variables (.env)

```
# API Configuration
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8080/api
VITE_API_TIMEOUT=30000

# Application Configuration
VITE_APP_NAME=AASA
VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0

# Feature Flags
VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true
VITE_ENABLE_NOTIFICATIONS=true
```

## Production Environment Variables

### Backend (.env.production)
```
# Gemini API Configuration
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_production_gemini_api_key

# JWT Configuration (CHANGE THIS!)
JWT_SECRET=your_production_jwt_secret_key_minimum_32_characters_required

# Database Configuration (Production)
DATABASE_URL=jdbc:postgresql://prod-db.example.com:5432/aasa_db_prod
DATABASE_USER=prod_aasa_user
DATABASE_PASSWORD=your_secure_production_password

# Server Configuration
SERVER_PORT=8080
SERVER_SERVLET_CONTEXT_PATH=/

# JPA/Hibernate Configuration
JPA_HIBERNATE_DDL_AUTO=validate
JPA_SHOW_SQL=false

# File Upload Configuration
FILE_UPLOAD_DIR=/var/aasa/uploads
FILE_MAX_SIZE=52428800

# CORS Configuration (Production)
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com,https://www.yourdomain.com
CORS_ALLOWED_METHODS=GET,POST,PUT,DELETE,OPTIONS
CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS=true

# Logging Configuration
LOGGING_LEVEL_ROOT=WARN
LOGGING_LEVEL_COM_AASA=INFO
LOGGING_FILE=/var/log/aasa/application.log
LOGGING_FILE_MAX_SIZE=10MB
LOGGING_FILE_MAX_HISTORY=30

# SSL Configuration
SERVER_SSL_ENABLED=true
SERVER_SSL_KEY_STORE=/etc/ssl/aasa/keystore.jks
SERVER_SSL_KEY_STORE_PASSWORD=your_keystore_password
SERVER_SSL_KEY_STORE_TYPE=JKS
```

### Frontend (.env.production)
```
# API Configuration
VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com/api
VITE_API_TIMEOUT=30000

# Application Configuration
VITE_APP_NAME=AASA
VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0

# Feature Flags
VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true
VITE_ENABLE_NOTIFICATIONS=true

# Analytics
VITE_ANALYTICS_ID=your_analytics_id
```

## Docker Environment Variables

### docker-compose.yml
```yaml
environment:
  # Backend
  SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL: jdbc:postgresql://postgres:5432/aasa_db
  SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME: aasa_user
  SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD: aasa_password
  GEMINI_API_KEY: ${GEMINI_API_KEY}
  JWT_SECRET: ${JWT_SECRET}

  # Frontend
  VITE_API_URL: http://localhost:8080/api
```

## Setup Instructions

### 1. Backend Setup
```bash
cd backend

# Copy template
cp .env.example .env

# Edit with your values
nano .env

# Required values:
# - GEMINI_API_KEY (get from Google AI Studio)
# - JWT_SECRET (generate a secure key)
# - DATABASE credentials (if not using default)
```

### 2. Frontend Setup
```bash
cd frontend

# Copy template
cp .env.example .env

# Edit with your values
nano .env

# Verify API URL matches backend
```

### 3. Obtaining Gemini API Key

1. Go to [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com)
2. Click "Get API Key"
3. Create a new API key
4. Copy the key
5. Add to `.env` file:
   ```
   GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key_here
   ```

### 4. Generating JWT Secret

```bash
# Generate secure random key
openssl rand -base64 32

# Or use Python
python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"

# Or use Node.js
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
```

### 5. Database Configuration

```bash
# Default credentials (development)
DATABASE_URL=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/aasa_db
DATABASE_USER=aasa_user
DATABASE_PASSWORD=aasa_password

# For production, use strong password:
# - Minimum 16 characters
# - Mix of uppercase, lowercase, numbers, special characters
```

## Security Best Practices

### 1. JWT Secret
- ✅ Minimum 32 characters
- ✅ Use cryptographically secure random generation
- ✅ Never commit to version control
- ✅ Rotate periodically in production

### 2. Database Password
- ✅ Minimum 16 characters
- ✅ Mix of character types
- ✅ No dictionary words
- ✅ Use password manager

### 3. API Keys
- ✅ Never commit to repository
- ✅ Use environment variables
- ✅ Rotate regularly
- ✅ Monitor usage

### 4. CORS Configuration
- ✅ Whitelist only trusted domains
- ✅ Use HTTPS in production
- ✅ Disable credentials if not needed
- ✅ Review regularly

## Environment Validation

### Backend
```bash
# Check if all required variables are set
mvn spring-boot:run

# Should see:
# - Database connection successful
# - Gemini API initialized
# - Server started on port 8080
```

### Frontend
```bash
# Check if API URL is correct
npm run dev

# Should see:
# - Vite dev server running
# - API calls working
# - No CORS errors
```

## Troubleshooting

### Missing Environment Variable
```
Error: GEMINI_API_KEY not found
Solution: Add to .env file and restart application
```

### Invalid JWT Secret
```
Error: JWT token invalid
Solution: Ensure JWT_SECRET is at least 32 characters
```

### Database Connection Failed
```
Error: Cannot connect to database
Solution: Verify DATABASE_URL and credentials
```

### CORS Error
```
Error: CORS policy blocked request
Solution: Add frontend URL to CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS
```

## Environment Checklist

### Development
- [ ] `.env` file created
- [ ] GEMINI_API_KEY set
- [ ] JWT_SECRET set (any value)
- [ ] Database running
- [ ] Backend starts without errors
- [ ] Frontend starts without errors
- [ ] API calls working

### Production
- [ ] `.env.production` created
- [ ] GEMINI_API_KEY set (production key)
- [ ] JWT_SECRET set (secure, 32+ chars)
- [ ] DATABASE_URL points to production DB
- [ ] CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS set correctly
- [ ] SSL/HTTPS configured
- [ ] Logging configured
- [ ] Backups configured
- [ ] Monitoring configured

## Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Create .env file
cd backend
cp .env.example .env

# 2. Add your Gemini API key
# Edit .env and add: GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key

# 3. Start backend
mvn spring-boot:run

# 4. In another terminal, start frontend
cd frontend
npm run dev

# 5. Open browser
# http://localhost:3000
```

---

**Remember**: Never commit `.env` files to version control!
